{
  "case_id": "2006-05-908",
  "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Harry J.F. Korrell",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KORRELL: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court. In an effort to achieve its desired racial balance in its popular high schools, the Seattle school district denied over 300 children, both white and minority children, admission to their chosen schools solely because of their race and without any individualized consideration. This strikes at the heart of the Equal Protection Clause which commands that Government treat people as individuals, not simply as members of a racial class."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0000-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Seattle school district denied over 300 children, both white and minority children, admission to their chosen schools solely because of their race and without any individualized consideration."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do you disagree in general with the Solicitor General's brief? Do you agree in general with the brief submitted by the Government or do you have differences with it in its approach?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Clement",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0000-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL CLEMENT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Respondents assert an interest in addressing the most racially isolated schools in the district, yet their plan does not address the two most racially concentrated high schools in their district. They likewise have certain interests in diversity, yet their plan does not directly address diversity other than pure racial diversity, and they do nothing to assemble the kind of critical mass that was at issue in the Grutter case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would that be impermissible, to have a mix of teachers in all the schools?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General Clement, is there anything unconstitutional about desiring a mingling of the races and establishing policies which achieve that result but which do not single out individuals and disqualify them for certain things because of their race? Is there anything wrong with a policy of wanting to have racial mix?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My question is really Judge Boudin's question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is there anything unconstitutional about that objective?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael F. Madden (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would say not, because housing decisions are inherently private, unlike public education."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael F. Madden (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that is roughly the circumstance that existed in the first Seattle case, Mr. Chief Justice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael F. Madden (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that the term racial balancing has two significant meanings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Madden",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let's take Franklin High School to begin with. In, in 2000, that school was -- had 25 percent white enrollment. In 2005, it had 10 percent white enrollment. In the ninth grade, which is really the, the level at which we see the effect of the segregation tie breaker, in 2000, the white enrollment was 21 percent; it was 8 percent in 2005."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I mean, have you gone back to square one? And it's just, there's no diversity at all? Or is there substantially more diversity? Can you tell us about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: How do, how do you square your objective of achieving racial balance with your disinterest in the situation at Cleveland and Rainier Beach? Those are the most unbalanced schools under your definition, and yet those are not affected at all by this plan. Why, why are you not concerned about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Madden",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9bed12dbcb18-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do not mandate that a student attend a school for integration purposes as we once did."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-908",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "9bed12dbcb18c32ab91ebb8a0c41764f9837d4df1b7a7f3b4e0e1feb73ec8493",
